d on the number of ones in binary representation and then by decimal value.\\n\\nComplexity:\\n- Counting ones in binary: O(n) for each number, where n is the number of bits.\\n- Sorting: O(m log m), where m is the number of elements in the list.\\n\\nThis algorithm ensures the function meets the specified requirements and handles edge cases appropriately."}'}]
